Initial conditions: parametric NSM-ejecta trajectories for WinNet
=================================================================

Free parameters per trajectory: Ye0, s0 [kB/baryon], v_inf [c].
Fixed: T0 = 7 GK, R0 = 50 km.

  rho0 : solves s_ion(NSE) + s_e+-(T0, rho Ye) + s_gamma(T0, rho) = s0
         NSE from WinNet's own nuclear data (../Nuclear_data/winvne_v2.0.dat),
         e+- and photon entropy from the Helmholtz EOS (Timmes & Swesty 2000).
  tau  : e R0 / (3 v_inf)   (late homologous branch moves at v_inf)
  rho(t) = rho0 exp(-t/tau)            t <= 3 tau
         = rho0 (3 tau / (e t))^3      t >= 3 tau
  R(t)   = R0 (rho0 / rho)^(1/3)

Files
-----
initial_state.py     NSE solver (winvne), ion entropy, Helmholtz wrapper, rho0 root find
make_ensemble.py     Sobol sample (2^10) of (Ye0, s0, v_inf) -> Trajectories_ensemble/
plot_rho0_map.py     heat maps of rho0 and NSE composition on (s0, Ye0) -> ../Figures/
rho0_grid_T7GK.npz   cached grid for the heat maps
HelmholtzEOS/        Timmes Helmholtz EOS; run_helm.f90 = batch entropy driver
Trajectories_ensemble/  trajNNNN.dat (time[s] T9 rho[g/cm3] R[km] Ye) + trajectories_index.csv

Run (from this folder, with the project venv ../.venv)
---
../.venv/bin/python make_ensemble.py           # ~2 min
../.venv/bin/python plot_rho0_map.py           # add --recompute to rebuild the grid (~1 min)

Build run_helm.exe (if needed), in HelmholtzEOS/:
awk 'NR>43' helmholtz.f90 > .helm_lib.f90 && gfortran -O2 -ffree-line-length-none run_helm.f90 .helm_lib.f90 -o run_helm.exe && rm .helm_lib.f90
